src/oracles/Curve2TokenOracle.sol:_lpTokenValue:73|C2|High|_lpTokenValue() reads ICurvePool(LP_TOKEN).balances(0/1) and ERC20(LP_TOKEN).totalSupply() with no Curve reentrancy-lock probe (the vault-side _checkReentrancyContext() pattern is absent and cannot be used from a view), so an attacker who calls remove_liquidity on an ETH-holding Curve pool and re-enters from the raw-ETH transfer callback sees totalSupply already burned and coin-1's balances not yet decremented — inflating tokenClaim for that leg by 1/(1-f) — while the get_dy deviation band stays satisfied because a high-A stableswap moves spot far less than the reserve imbalance, letting them mint/borrow against an LP price inflated by several percent for only round-trip Curve fees.|src/oracles/Curve2TokenOracle.sol
